# GEMV y = A(2048x2048) * x(2048), GDDR6 method 2: keep partial sum in accumulator.
# Mapping assumption:
# - GDDR6 maps 2048 matrix rows as 4 output batches over 32 channels x 16 banks.
# - Each output batch uses row 2*b for columns 0..1023 and row 2*b+1 for columns 1024..2047.
# - For each output batch, load vector half 0, compute first half, load vector half 1,
#   then continue MAC without RD_MAC or WR_BIAS between halves.
# - This avoids GPR partial-sum traffic but reloads both vector halves for every output batch.
# - GPR0 stores vector half 0, GPR64 stores vector half 1, GPR128 stores zero bias.
# - GPR512+b receives final outputs for output batch b.
AiM WR_GB 64 0 0xffffffff
W CFR 0 1
AiM WR_BIAS 128 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 0
AiM WR_GB 64 64 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 1
AiM RD_MAC 512 0xffffffff
AiM WR_GB 64 0 0xffffffff
AiM WR_BIAS 128 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 2
AiM WR_GB 64 64 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 3
AiM RD_MAC 513 0xffffffff
AiM WR_GB 64 0 0xffffffff
AiM WR_BIAS 128 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 4
AiM WR_GB 64 64 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 5
AiM RD_MAC 514 0xffffffff
AiM WR_GB 64 0 0xffffffff
AiM WR_BIAS 128 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 6
AiM WR_GB 64 64 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 64 0xffffffff 7
AiM RD_MAC 515 0xffffffff
AiM ISR_EOC
